{
  "slug": "python-clean-architecture",
  "name": "Python Clean Architecture",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Scaffold, review, and refactor Python projects with clean code and architecture. Design principles and patterns implemented the Pythonic way — using Protocol, Callable, functools.partial, and closures instead of heavy class hierarchies. Includes a /review-architecture command, layered FastAPI project scaffolding, and reference guides for 7 design principles, 17 code quality rules, and 10 Pythonic pattern recipes. Inspired by Arjan Codes.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **13 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `clean-architecture` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"scaffold a FastAPI project\", \"set up clean architecture\",…)\n- **Commands** (13): `add-endpoint` (Scaffold a new endpoint across all three architecture layers), `check-quality` (Quick code quality check against the 22 design rules), `decouple` (Find tight coupling and suggest dependency injection improvements), `diagnose-smells` (Detect code smells and anti-patterns with fix suggestions), `extract-god-class` (Find and split god classes into focused collaborators), `learn-architecture` (Learn an architecture or design topic — theory, the Pythonic way, and how it applies in your code), `make-pythonic` (Refactor code to use Pythonic patterns), `refactor-legacy` (Plan a safe refactoring path for untested legacy code), and 5 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install python-clean-architecture@claude-community` from `MKToronto/python-clean-architecture`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
